// The project manifest for the Cadenza iterators library, written in Cadenza itself.
// `cdz` reads these well-known top-level defs to know how to build / run / test the project.
//
//   cdz test          — search up for this Project.cdz and run its suite (like cargo)
//   cdz test .        — same, naming this directory
//
// Extracted from the compiler-ml package (operator directive 2026-07-18) so compiler-ml stays
// laser-focused on the integer spine; the iterator library is a pure prelude-only consumer with no
// dependency on the compiler pipeline, so it lives as its own sibling package (like cad / agent-harness).

def name = "iterators"

// The iterator library modules — every source file under src/ (a wildcard, so a new combinator module
// just drops into src/ and is picked up automatically). Today: iter.cdz (monomorphic-Int64 reified
// pull-iterator + range family), giter.cdz (generic strict cons-cell iterator), giter-flat.cdz (nested
// flatten). The monomorphic/generic/fusing adapter-record redesign (operator re-charter) lands here too.
def modules = ["src/*.cdz"]

// The modules whose `@test` definitions form the suite. Same-file with their code (a cross-file test
// cannot yet construct a type whose variant shadows a prelude name — see the shared issue queue).
def tests = ["src/*.cdz"]

// Files removed from the globs above. Empty — every src/*.cdz is a real library module.
def exclude = []
